# Al - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * Al.ugur.ang Al
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 does not vanish at rcut2, it stops at -50.8 meV (1.99 of k_B T at 296 K).  USE for static properties and for lattice dynamics: measured against the measured dispersion the hard sets average 9.7 % over the 33 elements that have one, against 12.6 % for the switched sets, and are closer in 25 of them.  DO NOT use for molecular dynamics: copper, whose step is 8.4 meV, drifts 176 meV/atom/ns in NVE and heats from 306 K to 389 K in 40 ps
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K the crystal collapses: it reaches 836 K and its potential energy falls below the static lattice.  Static properties from this set are still valid.
#
# LATTICE STABILITY: this set is NOT a harmonic minimum.
# Along the Setyawan-Curtarolo path its frequencies reach -3.446 cm^-1,
# with 0.40 % of the sampled modes imaginary.  That is a separate
# failure from the 600 K screen above and is not covered by it.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Al at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Al Al Al 16.9689315085662 0.26549617634916184 0.14251556936694787 3.9408618706436349 0.78938377281165018 -0.4999778170573656 0.089562255835741955 10.528700000000001 4.2951433656223861 -1 -0.94999261785518119 0.59488662063208431
